WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.280
"The Benefits of Fenugreek for
Preventing and Treating Diabetes"

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.760
The spice fenugreek is
considered to be one of

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:18.000
humanity’s oldest medicinal plants.
What can it do?

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.040
In my last video on fenugreek,
I explored the evidence showing

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.499
it can improve sexual
function in both men and women,

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.080
decrease menstrual pain,

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.800
and boost milk production
in lactating mothers.

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:31.360
And what are the side effects?

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.560
Fifteen randomized controlled
trials show, on average,

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.160
a significant improvement
in cholesterol levels.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.640
And a dozen other studies show
significant improvements

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.920
in both long- and short-term blood
sugar control in diabetics

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.240
and prediabetics using an average of
about a half teaspoon a day

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:51.374
over a period of an
average of two months.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.040
Results clearly indicate that
fenugreek is an inexpensive,

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:57.520
low-risk dietary supplement
that has potential

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:00.828
to improve blood sugar
control in diabetes.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:05.040
What exactly is the mechanism by
which it lowers blood sugars?

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:09.280
There’s a peculiar amino
acid in fenugreek

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.280
that increases insulin
release from the pancreas.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:17.520
The peculiar 4-hydroxyisoleucine
has been described as

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.760
an efﬁcient compound in the
regulation of insulin secretion.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.000
Due to the fact that it
acts as a secretagogue

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.520
in the presence of elevated
blood glucose concentrations,

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.720
it has been proposed for
the potential treatment

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:35.120
of insulin resistance,
diabetes, and obesity.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.120
There’s a class of diabetes drugs
that does the same thing:

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:42.000
sulfonylureas, sold as like Glucotrol,

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.880
glyburide, Micronase, glipizide.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.000
The problem is that they
increase insulin secretion

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.920
whether you need it or not,

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.600
and so there’s a risk
of severe hypoglycemia,

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.080
driving your blood sugars too low.

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:59.280
The funky fenugreek amino
acid, on the other hand,

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.360
only boosts it when you need it.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.920
When your blood sugars are
normal, it has no effect.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.400
It only seems to stimulate
extra insulin release

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.760
when you need it most, when
your blood sugars are high.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:12.800
What these researchers did,
was after consent was obtained

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:15.600
from family members,
pancreases were obtained

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.840
from brain-dead organ donors.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:20.400
Put the insulin-secreting
cells in a petri dish

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.720
at a low blood sugar concentration,

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.160
and they release a little insulin,

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.440
and at high blood sugar levels
they release more insulin.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.520
That makes sense.
That’s what they’re supposed to do,

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.160
since insulin is the
hormone your body releases

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.800
when trying to bring
down your blood sugars.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.600
Add in some of that
fenugreek amino acid, though,

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.800
and you can boost insulin
production. Great!

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:44.560
But if that happened even at the
low blood sugar concentration too,

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.040
it would be like the drugs
and you could dip too low,

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:52.640
but no, when you don’t need extra
insulin, no fenugreek effect.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.160
What about the role of fenugreek

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:57.360
in the prevention of type 2 diabetes?

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.480
A 3-year randomized controlled
study of the efficacy

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.426
of fenugreek on men and women
diagnosed with prediabetes.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.000
Those randomized to fenugreek
were told to take about

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.240
one and a third teaspoons of
fenugreek powder twice a day

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.560
before meals, and both the fenugreek

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.120
and the control groups that
didn’t get any fenugreek

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.920
were both given identical
diet and lifestyle advice.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:21.520
And, by the end of the study,
the cumulative incidence rate

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:26.080
of diabetes was reduced significantly
in the fenugreek group.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:29.120
Check it out. Those who didn’t
get the fenugreek

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.800
had a four times higher
chance of developing diabetes,

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.840
and you could already see
the groups starting to diverge

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:39.760
within six months, and all
from just a few cents worth

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.960
of a spice, every day.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:47.440
If you yourself want to
intimately support this kind of

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:48.960
amazing research in the future,

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:55.712
be sure to register at organdonor.gov.

